}
```

**Time**: O(n) instead of O(n²) with nested loops

### Iterative Approach (Best)
```java
Node reverse(Node head) {
    Node prev = null;
    Node current = head;
    while (current != null) {
        Node next = current.next;
        current.next = prev;
        prev = current;
        current = next;
    }
    return prev;
}
```

**Time:** O(n), **Space:** O(1)

### Recursive Approach
```java
Node reverse(Node head) {
    if (head == null || head.next == null) return head;
    Node rest = reverse(head.next);
    head.next.next = head;
    head.next = null;
    return rest;
}
```

**Time:** O(n), **Space:** O(n) due to recursion stack

### Search in BST
```java
boolean search(Node root, int key) {
    if (root == null) return false;
    if (root.data == key) return true;
    if (key < root.data) return search(root.left, key);
    return search(root.right, key);
}
```

### Insert in BST
```java
Node insert(Node root, int key) {
    if (root == null) return new Node(key);
    if (key < root.data) root.left = insert(root.left, key);
    else root.right = insert(root.right, key);
    return root;
}
```

**Time Complexity:**
- Average: O(log n)
- Worst (skewed tree): O(n)

Sliding Window optimizes problems involving subarrays/substrings.

### Example: Max sum of k consecutive elements
```java
int maxSum(int[] arr, int k) {
    int windowSum = 0, maxSum = 0;
    // First window
    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) windowSum += arr[i];
    maxSum = windowSum;

    // Slide window
    for (int i = k; i < arr.length; i++) {
        windowSum = windowSum - arr[i-k] + arr[i];
        maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, windowSum);
    }
    return maxSum;
}
```

**Time:** O(n) instead of O(n*k) with nested loops

**Use cases:** Longest substring, maximum sum subarray

### Approach 1: Two Pointers
```java
boolean isPalindrome(String s) {
    int left = 0, right = s.length() - 1;
    while (left < right) {
        if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right))
            return false;
        left++;
        right--;
    }
    return true;
}
```
**Time:** O(n), **Space:** O(1)

### Approach 2: Reverse and Compare
```java
boolean isPalindrome(String s) {
    String reversed = new StringBuilder(s).reverse().toString();
    return s.equals(reversed);
}
```
**Time:** O(n), **Space:** O(n)

### BFS (Breadth-First Search)
- **Level-by-level** traversal
- Uses **Queue**
- Finds shortest path
```java
void BFS(Node start) {
    Queue<Node> queue = new LinkedList<>();
    Set<Node> visited = new HashSet<>();
    queue.add(start);

    while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
        Node node = queue.poll();
        if (!visited.contains(node)) {
            System.out.println(node.val);
            visited.add(node);
            queue.addAll(node.neighbors);
        }
    }
}
```

### DFS (Depth-First Search)
- **Deep dive** before backtrack
- Uses **Stack** (or recursion)
```java
void DFS(Node node, Set<Node> visited) {
    if (visited.contains(node)) return;
    System.out.println(node.val);
    visited.add(node);
    for (Node neighbor : node.neighbors) {
        DFS(neighbor, visited);
    }
}
```

**Use BFS:** Shortest path, level-order
**Use DFS:** Connectivity, cycle detection
